## About Me
I am a physical security professional with a strong interest in cybersecurity and network security, currently building hands-on technical skills alongside my professional role. 
My learning journey focuses on practical system hardening, traffic analysis, and SOC-style incident response through structured labs and real-world simulations.
I am actively developing expertise in Linux security, packet capture and analysis, and log-based threat detection, with a long-term goal of contributing to secure, resilient, and mission-critical network environments. 
This portfolio reflects my commitment to disciplined learning, ethical security practices, and continuous technical growth in the field of network defense and cyber operations.
